# Binary assets must never go through line-ending conversion.
# core.autocrlf=true on the Windows machines was rewriting LF to CRLF inside
# PDFs on checkout, which changes their byte length and can corrupt a file that
# is later committed back from that working copy. Print files are the ones that
# actually hurt: a mangled PDF still returns 200 and still opens as "a PDF",
# so nothing tells you it broke until it is on a print shop counter.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
